Target-header and integer NEON targeted replay, 2026-09-19.
This is not a complete application campaign, kernel installation or boot.
Fixed image: evo-flight-lab:sealed, linux/arm64, network none.
Image digest: 2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2.
Oracles: GCC 14.2.0-19 and Clang 19.1.7; GNU11, O0/O2.

No replacement arm_neon.h is used. Subject include paths come from the
existing tools/ladder/e0.py include_flags over .build/ladder/sysroot.
The GCC14 vendor header is parsed, including otherwise unused inline bodies.
The frozen target's nominal types/private builtin spellings are a GCC-header
profile, not a claim that Clang exposes GCC's private interface.

Interface extraction:
  container run --rm --platform linux/arm64 --network none -v "$PWD:/work:ro" \
    evo-flight-lab:sealed python3 /work/tools/extract-aarch64-builtins.py \
    --seed /work/crates/evocc-types/src/neon-signatures.tsv
  exit 0; 2,980 unique prototypes; stdout equals checked-in TSV byte-for-byte.
  SHA256 d936c48b70199f4dcf7d4c1403070f4beb619b049b952961a2190647925e15ca.
  This includes 450 public reinterpret prototypes injected by GCC's pragma;
  same-type identity spellings are not declared by that pragma.
  90 tuple typedefs are ordinary records with a val array, not opaque sizes.

