SIMD assembly contract gap, arm-neon-assembly.c:
  gcc-14/clang-19 at O0/O2: build 0, run 0 (4 runs).
  Current Section 3.11 explicitly refuses constraints outside its table;
    w/=w is not in that table. xor-neon.c:188 needs =w/w for eor3.
  Retain E3021; do not select general registers for SIMD operands or replace
    a particular assembly template with guessed C semantics.

Immediate boundary probe:
  vshrq_n_u8(a,0x100000001ULL): both fixed compilers O0 build/run 0;
    GCC warns that conversion to int changes 4294967297 to 1.
  Private __builtin_aarch64_lshrv16qi_uus has the same measured GCC behavior.
  vshrq_n_u8(a,(0,1)): GCC accepts/runs 0, Clang refuses non-constant argument.
    Source ICE requirement is retained; do not substitute optimizer folding.
  Before repair, the private wide-constant case reports E3063 in both subject
    interpreters and assembly emission: a declared failing case, not a build error.
  After applying declared-parameter conversion in both consumers, the dedicated
    Rust regression passes C-HIR, EvoIR interpretation and assembly emission.
  arm-neon-immediate-conversion.c also passes both fixed oracles at O0/O2;
    GCC warns on 4294967297 -> 1 and 4294967303 -> 7, Clang emits no warning.

