Gate follow-up and diagnostic allocation:
  The first broad gate completed 2,498 PASS, 2 FAIL, 4 historical ignored.
  Both failures were stale expectations after replacing the opaque float
    vector with its actual lane type: DWARF's anonymous vector DIE and E3050.
  The tests now follow the typedef to its element/count and pin the named
    floating-value diagnostic. The 59-test affected group passes.
  Independently, sealed gcc-14 assembly plus readelf confirms DW_TAG_array_type,
    DW_AT_GNU_vector=1, DW_AT_count=4 and a 4-byte DW_ATE_float element;
    the sizeless predicate remains DW_TAG_unspecified_type.
  The new target-builtin diagnostic is allocated as E3052 within the authorized
    E3042-E3059 interval. Earlier E3063 observations above retain their original
    spelling; they are not claims about the current code.
  Current release SHA256:
    4bc75461c69a599043363d462f2bd415be10a0a6033f86791689c9026072dc94.
